/Title (The hotel loan shows clear distress with a notice of default provided in July, even as the borrower continues to pursue a sale or refinancing. The Denver office tower loan advanced toward foreclosure in September. A court-appointed receiver took control of the property after the borrower indicated it would give up the asset. The Silicon Valley office loan exhausted its extension options and missed its maturity in August, moving directly from current to foreclosure.)
