/Title (The month's largest cure was a $384.3 million Los Angeles office tower that moved from non-performing to performing matured balloon status after the borrower resumed making interest-only payments. Three large regional malls cured or paid off this month, including a $260.1 million mall in Lakewood, California, and a $210.0 million mall near Rochester, New York, that turned to performing matured balloon status, and a $232.9 million mall in Providence, Rhode Island, that paid off in full.)
